{
  "name": "EXPRESS-Bench probe (built-in navigator)",
  "description": "EXPRESS-Bench wiring probe assembled from built-in glue (llmCall, textParse, historyLog) + basic_agent image_analyze + the env_express nodeset's verbs. Loop: observe -> caption -> LLM proposes a free-pose waypoint JSON -> step_pose (navmesh-snapped teleport, path length accumulated). After the loop (budget truncation or bad-action stop) the verdict band answers the question from the FINAL frame only (mirrors upstream Fine-EQA's single-frame answering), assembles the benchmark's judge prompt via env_express__judge_prompt, judges with an llmCall (use a gpt-4o-mini profile on the judge node for benchmark-native scoring - profiles are user-level, never baked into the JSON), and env_express__evaluate folds delta/sigma with path efficiency + goal distance into C / C* / E_path / d_T. No method-specific code - this graph exists to exercise env_express end-to-end; scores are not competitive (paper reference: Fine-EQA C 40.55 / E_path 16.22).",
  "step_budget": 50,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "env_reset",
      "type": "env_express__reset",
      "label": "EXPRESS: Reset",
      "position": { "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "config": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "seed_obs",
      "type": "env_express__observe_egocentric",
      "label": "EXPRESS: Observe (seed)",
      "position": { "x": 0, "y": 220 },
      "config": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "iter_in",
      "type": "iterIn",
      "label": "Iteration Gate",
      "position": { "x": 280, "y": 200 },
      "config": {
        "version": 3,
        "pairedWith": "iter_out",
        "initPorts": [
          {
            "name": "question",
            "wire_type": "TEXT",
            "persist": true,
            "required": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "caption",
      "type": "basic_agent__image_analyze",
      "label": "Vision: Analyze",
      "position": { "x": 560, "y": 320 },
      "config": {
        "temperature": 1.0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "planner_llm",
      "type": "llmCall",
      "label": "LLM: Propose Waypoint",
      "position": { "x": 840, "y": 200 },
      "config": {
        "ports": [
          {
            "name": "question",
            "wire_type": "TEXT",
            "required": true
          },
          {
            "name": "caption",
            "wire_type": "TEXT",
            "required": true
          },
          {
            "name": "position_normal",
            "wire_type": "ANY",
            "required": true
          },
          {
            "name": "angle",
            "wire_type": "ANY",
            "required": true
          },
          {
            "name": "history",
            "wire_type": "TEXT",
            "required": false
          }
        ],
        "template": "You are exploring an indoor scene to answer: {question}\n\nWhat you currently see: {caption}\n\nYour position in the map frame is {position_normal} (x, y, floor_height) and your yaw is {angle} radians.\n\nWaypoints already visited:\n{history}\n\nPropose the next exploration waypoint. Move at most 3 metres per hop. Prefer unexplored directions; if the view is a wall or dead end, turn toward open space. Give one short sentence of reasoning, then write on the last line ONLY a JSON object of the form {\"position_normal\": [x, y], \"angle\": yaw_radians} - no code fences, no other text on that line.",
        "system_prompt": "You are an embodied exploration agent inside an indoor environment. You explore efficiently toward answering a question about the scene.",
        "profile": "",
        "temperature": 1.0,
        "max_tokens": 2000,
        "mode": "single_turn"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "parse_action",
      "type": "textParse",
      "label": "Parse Waypoint JSON",
      "position": { "x": 1120, "y": 200 },
      "config": {
        "mode": "regex",
        "pattern": "\\{[^{}]*\\}",
        "default": ""
      }
    },
    {
