    {
      "id": "note_probe",
      "type": "note",
      "label": "env_express probe graph",
      "position": { "x": 560, "y": -340 },
      "config": {
        "markdown": "**EXPRESS-Bench from built-in parts only**\n\nEvery reasoning node ships with the platform (`llmCall`, `textParse`, `historyLog`) plus the `basic_agent` captioner. The env side is `env_express`'s verbs: reset / observe_egocentric / step_pose / judge_prompt / evaluate.\n\n**Action contract** - `step_pose` takes free-pose JSON `{\"position_normal\": [x, y], \"angle\": rad}`; the waypoint is navmesh-snapped and the geodesic hop distance accumulates into `path_len` (drives E_path). A hop is capped at 3 m by prompt, mirroring upstream's planner limit.\n\n**Verdict band** (fires once, off `final_*`): answer from the FINAL frame only (upstream Fine-EQA answers from a single frame too) -> `judge_prompt` assembles the benchmark's evaluation.txt prompt with GT answer -> judge llmCall returns `delta, sigma` (grounding FIRST) -> `evaluate` computes C / C* / E_path / d_T.\n\n**Judge model**: the benchmark judges with **gpt-4o-mini**. Select a gpt-4o-mini profile on the judge node at run time - profiles are user-level and never baked into graph JSON.\n\n**Scope**: wiring probe, not a competitive method (paper reference: Fine-EQA C 40.55 / C* 63.95 / E_path 16.22 / d_T 6.43).\n\n**Episode selection** is env-panel-owned (split val/train/all -> episode)."
      }
    }
  ],
